Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos9830-ems: keep big cores for mid overflow

EMS ontime migration moves a task from the mid cluster (Cortex-A76) to
the big cluster (Mongoose M5) once its runnable load reaches the mid
domain's upper boundary, and back when it falls below the big domain's
lower boundary.  The stock boundaries (586 and 205 out of 1024) send any
task that uses a little over half of a mid core to the big cores, which
are the least efficient cores of the SoC.

Raise the mid upper boundary to 820 and the big lower boundary to 500 in
the everyday modes (normal, power-scenario, balance, light-video and
pinned), so only tasks that nearly saturate a mid core migrate to the big
cluster, and they return once the load drops.  Sets without their own
ontime block (such as "normal med boost", used while scrolling) inherit
these values from their mode's default set.

The big boost sets (app launch and heavy load boosts) and the
performance, light-game and game modes keep the stock boundaries.
